  "result": "I changed the keyset resume predicate in `src/server/repositories/_paging.ts` so that \"Load more\" no longer drops rows that share a timestamp.\n\nThe cause: every list orders by `(sortColumn DESC, id DESC)`, but `keysetPredicate` resumed with only `sortColumn < cursorValue`. When a bulk import or a burst of assignments writes many rows in the same millisecond, the rows at a page boundary that share the cursor's timestamp were excluded from the next page. That is why the count in the header and the pages disagreed.\n\nThe predicate now matches the ordering: `sortColumn < v OR (sortColumn = v AND id < lastId)`. It is shared by the issue, project, notification, activity, comment, member and search listings, so they all get the fix. The org filter is still applied in each repository, so cross-workspace leakage is unchanged.\n\nI haven't run the test suite.",
